            korean: `<p><span class="korean-word" data-translation="last spring" data-pronunciation="지난 봄 [jinan bom]">지난 봄</span> <span class="korean-word" data-translation="the Cultural Heritage Administration" data-pronunciation="문화재청 [munhwajaecheong]">문화재청</span><span class="korean-word" data-translation="invited" data-pronunciation="은 초청했습니다 [eun chocheonghaetseumnida]">은 초청했습니다</span> <span class="korean-word" data-translation="master artisans" data-pronunciation="장인 [jang-in]">장인</span><span class="korean-word" data-translation="and" data-pronunciation="과 [gwa]">과</span> <span class="korean-word" data-translation="sound designers" data-pronunciation="사운드 디자이너 [saundeu dijaineo]">사운드 디자이너</span><span class="korean-word" data-translation="to create" data-pronunciation="를 제작하기 위해 [reul jejakhagi wihae]">를 제작하기 위해</span> <span class="korean-word" data-translation="a sound map of intangible urban heritage" data-pronunciation="도시 무형문화의 음향 지도 [dosi muhyeong munhwa-ui eumhyang jido]">도시 무형문화의 음향 지도</span>.</p>
<p><span class="korean-word" data-translation="in the juniper alley of Jongno" data-pronunciation="종로의 향나무 골목에서는 [jongno-ui hyangnamu golmok-eseoneun]">종로의 향나무 골목에서는</span> <span class="korean-word" data-translation="the sound of carving candles" data-pronunciation="향초를 깎는 칼소리가 [hyangchoreul gakkneun kalsoriga]">향초를 깎는 칼소리가</span> <span class="korean-word" data-translation="was recorded" data-pronunciation="녹음되었고 [nogeumdoe-eotgo]">녹음되었고</span>, <span class="korean-word" data-translation="at Hwanghak-dong market" data-pronunciation="황학동 시장에서는 [hwanghakdong sijang-eseoneun]">황학동 시장에서는</span> <span class="korean-word" data-translation="the rhythm of hand sewing" data-pronunciation="손바느질 리듬을 [sonbaneujil rideumeul]">손바느질 리듬을</span> <span class="korean-word" data-translation="as layers" data-pronunciation="레이어로 [reieoro]">레이어로</span> <span class="korean-word" data-translation="archived" data-pronunciation="겹쳐 아카이브했습니다 [gyeopchyeo akaibeuhaetseumnida]">겹쳐 아카이브했습니다</span>. <span class="korean-word" data-translation="in the Sadang station underpass" data-pronunciation="사당역 지하에서는 [sadang-yeok jiha-eseoneun]">사당역 지하에서는</span> <span class="korean-word" data-translation="a traditional drum" data-pronunciation="전통 북을 [jeontong bugeul]">전통 북을</span> <span class="korean-word" data-translation="with digital sensors" data-pronunciation="디지털 센서와 [dijiteol senseowa]">디지털 센서와</span> <span class="korean-word" data-translation="connected" data-pronunciation="연결해 [yeongyeolhae]">연결해</span> <span class="korean-word" data-translation="and held a public sound performance" data-pronunciation="공공 사운드 퍼포먼스를 진행했습니다 [gonggong saundeu peopomeonseureul jinhaenghaetseumnida]">공공 사운드 퍼포먼스를 진행했습니다</span>.</p>
<p><span class="korean-word" data-translation="in the finished map" data-pronunciation="완성된 지도에는 [wanseongdoen jido-eneun]">완성된 지도에는</span> <span class="korean-word" data-translation="the frequencies of each sound" data-pronunciation="각 소리의 주파수와 [gak soriui jupasuwa]">각 소리의 주파수와</span> <span class="korean-word" data-translation="stories of heritage communities" data-pronunciation="전승 공동체의 이야기 [jeonseung gongdongche-ui iyagi]">전승 공동체의 이야기</span> <span class="korean-word" data-translation="as metadata" data-pronunciation="가 메타데이터로 [ga metadeiteoro]">가 메타데이터로</span> <span class="korean-word" data-translation="are linked" data-pronunciation="연결되었고 [yeongyeoldoeeotgo]">연결되었고</span>, <span class="korean-word" data-translation="a vibration version" data-pronunciation="진동 버전도 [jindong beojeondo]">진동 버전도</span> <span class="korean-word" data-translation="for people with hearing impairments" data-pronunciation="청각 장애인을 위해 [cheonggak jangaeineul wihae]">청각 장애인을 위해</span> <span class="korean-word" data-translation="was simultaneously released" data-pronunciation="동시에 공개되었습니다 [dongsie gonggaedoeeotseumnida]">동시에 공개되었습니다</span>.</p>`,
            translation: "Last spring, the Cultural Heritage Administration invited master artisans and sound designers to create a sound map of intangible urban heritage. In a Jongno alley, they recorded the sound of candle carving; at Hwanghak-dong market, they layered and archived hand-sewing rhythms; and in the Sadang station underpass, they connected a traditional drum to digital sensors for a public performance. The finished map links each sound's frequencies with community stories as metadata, and a vibration version was simultaneously released for people with hearing impairments.",
