            translation: "In Seoul's Bukchon district, hanok restoration is ongoing. But this is not simply building repair. Master Park says: 'Hanok is architecture in harmony with nature. Wood breathes and clay regulates moisture. When restoring, you must understand these principles.' Recently, young architects have been learning traditional techniques. They create spaces that connect the old and the new. This is the true continuation of cultural heritage.",
